For each test, we measure
1.	Primary node workload performance (TPS, QPS, etc)
2.	Read-replica workload performance  (TPS, QPS, etc) if the test runs workload on the read replica
3.	Lagging between the primary node and the replica node (using Paul’s script)
 
Test Set 1: No workload on the read replica, no warm-up on replica, primary node runs
1.	Read-only, write-only, read-write
2.	For each of the above mode, run number of threads 1, 16, 64, 256, 512, 1024
 
Test Set 2: Warm-up primary and replica simultaneously, then start primary node runs, and at the same time, start read-only workload on read-replica.
1.	Read-only, write-only, read-write
2.	For each of the above mode, run number of threads 1, 16, 64, 256, 512, 1024
3.	The number of threads of the read-only workload on the replica matches with the number of threads on the master.
